Apply to: gta6-video-reader / skill/scripts/bink2mp4.py
Purpose:   honor the GTA6X_PRESET environment variable so the encoder preset
           can be selected at runtime (gta6media convert --preset ...).
Default:   "medium" when the variable is unset (unchanged stock behavior).

--- a/skill/scripts/bink2mp4.py
+++ b/skill/scripts/bink2mp4.py
@@ -126,8 +126,9 @@
     if wav_path:
         cmd_ff += ["-i", str(Path(wav_path).resolve())]
-    cmd_ff += ["-c:v", "libx264", "-preset", "medium", "-crf", str(crf),
-               "-pix_fmt", "yuv420p"]
+    _preset = os.environ.get("GTA6X_PRESET", "medium")
+    cmd_ff += ["-c:v", "libx264", "-preset", _preset, "-crf", str(crf),
+               "-pix_fmt", "yuv420p"]
     if wav_path:
         cmd_ff += ["-c:a", "aac", "-shortest"]

Apply with:  patch -p1 < bink2mp4-preset.patch   (from the repo root of
gta6-video-reader), or apply the two-line edit manually.
